<title>FINLAND: FINVEST CONFIRMS 96 PROFIT, NIL DIVIDEND.</title>
<headline>FINVEST CONFIRMS 96 PROFIT, NIL DIVIDEND.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish capacitor and consulting group Finvest Oy said in a statement on Wednesday that its final 1996 results were unchanged from the preliminary data released earlier, and proposed no dividend.</p>
<p>It confirmed the 13.0 million markka profit after financial items, down from 81.7 million markka.  </p>
<p>Finvest repeated an earlier forecast that the result would</p>
<p>improve significantly in 1997 on 1996.</p>
<p>It gave the following final 1996 results:</p>
<p> Net sales					1,711.8 vs 1,636.3</p>
<p> Operating profit before depreciation     144.9 vs 187.2</p>
<p> Depreciation					84.2 vs 66.9</p>
<p> Operating profit				  60.7 vs 120.3</p>
<p> Net financial items		    charge 28.1 vs 37.2 charge</p>
<p> Investment participations	    charge 19.6 vs 1.4 charge</p>
<p> Profit after fin items			  13.0 vs 81.7</p>
<p> Extraordinary items		    charge 18.2 vs 3.3 charge</p>
<p> Loss before minorities, taxes		  5.2 vs 78.4 profit</p>
<p> Taxes						 14.5 vs 23.3</p>
<p> Minorities				    gain 1.3 vs 5.9 charge</p>
<p> Change in depreciation difference    gain 14.9 vs 43.1 charge</p>
<p> Net loss					     3.5 vs 19.7 profit</p>
<p> Earnings per share (markka)		   0.05 vs 0.70</p>
<p> Equity to assets ratio (percent)	    31.1 vs 36.4</p>
<p> Proposed dividend (markka)		     nil vs 0.20</p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 242</p>
